# New Dutch texts of the UI layer (vendor/ui) that no key had at 3b898e6: Windows Update (notes/claude/windows-update-gnome.md
# §10, plan.md D-G28). Owner: GW3; later Windows Update steps write theirs to notes/claude/baseline-additions-<step>.txt
# and the coordinator merges them here. The list of *changed* keys is tests/i18n/BASELINE-CHANGES.ui.
# Checked by: python3 -B -m unittest tests/i18n/test_update_mock_rows.py (this file lists exactly the rows that
#   python3 -B tools/i18n/check_ui.py --dict-diff tests/i18n/dict-nl-3b898e6.tsv reports as "added" in
#   apps/settings/pages/update*.js and in the registry's P(update-*) pages, with the same text).
# A new key in these files adds no line to an existing block of tests/i18n/baseline-nl.txt except where §3.9 says so
# (BASELINE-CHANGES.ui); the dump shows it on the new surfaces (settings.update-*, settings-update.*).
# One line per new key, tab-separated:
#   STEP<TAB>key:<file below vendor/ui/js>:<key><TAB><the nl text exactly; TSV escapes \n \t \\>
# exportName is GE1a's (a Dutch-only literal moved into the dictionary unchanged, BASELINE-CHANGES.ui header).
# Sources of the texts: the design's §3.2-§3.4 and §3.6 tables (nl and en together, en-GB, typographic ’).
